National Weather Service Grand Forks ND

1045 PM CDT Thu Aug 14 2025



Here are the Recreation Area Forecasts...



Wave height forecasts represent the average of the highest 33% of

waves that occur in a given period. Since the significant wave

height is an average of the largest waves, mariners should be

aware that many individual waves will be higher. 



For Devils Lake...



.REST OF TONIGHT...North winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 foot or

less. Mostly clear. Lows in the upper 50s. 

.FRIDAY...Northwest winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Mostly sunny. Highs in the 70s. 

.FRIDAY NIGHT...East winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 foot or less

building to 1 to 2 feet after midnight. Partly cloudy in the

evening then becoming mostly cloudy. Lows in the upper 50s. 





For the Upper and Lower Red Lakes...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Southwest winds around 10 mph shifting to the

northwest early in the morning. Waves 1 foot or less. Chance of

thunderstorms. Mostly cloudy. Lows in the mid 60s. 

.FRIDAY...Northwest winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Mostly sunny. Highs in the 70s. 

.FRIDAY NIGHT...Northeast winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or

less. Partly cloudy in the evening then becoming mostly cloudy.

Lows in the upper 50s. 





For Lake of the Woods...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Southwest winds 10 to 15 mph shifting to the

northwest after midnight. Waves 1 to 2 feet. Showers likely and

chance of thunderstorms in the late evening and early morning.

Mostly cloudy late in the evening then becoming partly cloudy.

Lows in the lower 60s. 

.FRIDAY...West winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or less. Sunny.

Highs 65 to 75. 

.FRIDAY NIGHT...Northeast winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 to 2 feet

subsiding to 1 foot or less after midnight. Partly cloudy in the

evening then becoming mostly cloudy. Lows in the upper 50s. 





