Grand Junction Aviation Discussion

Issued at 0211 UTC Friday, August 15, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 518 PM MDT Thu Aug 14 2025

Scattered showers and thunderstorms will continue to impact

eastern Utah and western Colorado through the next 3-6 hours.

These showers and storms have mainly produced gusty, erratic

outflow winds and occasional lightning. Even after these showers

taper off, mid level scattered to broken cloud cover will linger

through the night. Westerly to southwesterly winds this evening

will becoming light and terrain driven overnight, before once

again turning gusty and southwesterly to southerly tomorrow

afternoon. Widespread showers and thunderstorms are expected

tomorrow afternoon, with diminishing threats of gusty winds and

increasing concerns for heavy rain. Wildfire smoke also remains

a concern. VFR conditions will prevail, but drops to MVFR due to

wildfire smoke or heavy rainfall will be possible through the

period.





