Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2348 UTC Thursday, August 14, 2025



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 531 PM MDT Thu Aug 14 2025

High-based showers and isolated storms across northern, central, 

and western NM late today will continue drifting erratically north

and east with strong outflow winds and brief rain. Showers will 

taper off after 10pm followed by lingering mid level cloud decks 

for most of the night along and west of the central mt chain. A

more active day is on tap Friday with numerous SHRA/TSRA erupting

over all of the high terrain after 11am. This activity will move

northward around 10KT with brief heavy rainfall, strong outflow 

winds, and frequent lightning. Direct hits may produce MVFR vsbys

along with wind gusts near 40KT. The greatest storm coverage is

likely after 3pm. 



