Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Memphis TN

1131 PM CDT Thu Aug 14 2025



...New DISCUSSION, AVIATION, FIRE WEATHER...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Updated at 1116 PM CDT Thu Aug 14 2025



- Hot and humid conditions continue across the Mid-South. High

  temperatures will generally be in the mid 90s today, increasing

  to the upper 90s this weekend.



- A Heat Advisory is in effect both today over eastern Arkansas

  and northwest Mississippi and West Tennessee, where heat indices

  of 104 to 107 prevail.



- An isolated thunderstorm or two is expected Friday afternoon.

  Most of the Mid-South will see no rainfall.  



&&



.DISCUSSION...

(Tonight through next Thursday)

Issued at 1130 PM CDT Thu Aug 14 2025



The longwave trough responsible for our consecutive afternoon shower 

and thunderstorm coverage is nearly parallel along the Mississippi 

River at this hour. This slow moving trough will continue its 

eastward progression on Friday. As the trough gets further away from 

the area, coverage of showers and storms will decrease. Coverage 

should be generally confined to north Mississippi, but a few storms 

could sneak into West Tennessee. Lack of confidence in coverage does 

bring up the question of afternoon max heat index values. Another 

Heat Advisory will be in effect Friday from 11AM-7PM for the same

geographical region as the previous two days along with the some 

addition to northern and eastern extent. 



As the trough finally clears the area, high pressure will begin to 

build and looks to dominate the rest of the forecast period. A 

diurnally driven thunderstorm cannot be ruled out, but generally a 

dry, hot and humid forecast is anticipated. Current model output 

favors the ridge amplifying around 590 dam, allowing temperatures to 

soar into the mid to upper 90s with heat indices in the triple 

digits. Some portions of the Mid-South will need a heat advisory as 

heat indices climb above 105, but this will need evaluated daily. 



DNM



&&



.AVIATION...

(06Z TAFS)

Issued at 1130 PM CDT Thu Aug 14 2025



A few TSRA are expected again Friday afternoon, but with the

exception of TUP, coverage should below PROB30 mention threshold.

In the interim, areas of fog will likely develop at MKL and TUP once

mid and high level clouds thin. 



PWB



&&



.FIRE WEATHER...

Issued at 1130 PM CDT Thu Aug 14 2025



Hot and dry conditions will build into the Midsouth this week, 

persisting into early next week. Minimum daytime relative humidity

values will prevail below 50 percent, accompanied by light winds 

and drying fine fuels. 



&&



.MEG WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

AR...Heat Advisory from 11 AM to 7 PM CDT Friday for ARZ009-018-

     026>028-035-036-048-049-058.



MO...Heat Advisory from 11 AM to 7 PM CDT Friday for MOZ113-115.



MS...Heat Advisory from 11 AM to 7 PM CDT Friday for MSZ001-007-008-

     010>012-020-021.



TN...Heat Advisory from 11 AM to 7 PM CDT Friday for TNZ001-002-019-

     048-049-088.



&&



$$



PUBLIC FORECAST...CMA

AVIATION...PWB



